{
	"id": "promise-hides-errors",
	"text": "To see how Effect helps, we'll write the same function twice, beginning with the Promise version. slowDie rolls a die, waits for no reason, and then returns the result. We will then outlaw 4, and pronounce its rolling to be punishable by death. If that accursed numeral has appeared, we will throw a VeryBadRoll error. Nevertheless, it continues to type-check. TypeScript doesn't care. Our feeble human mind is solely responsible for tracking this.",
	"code": "async function slowDie(): Promise<number> {\n  const n = Math.ceil(Math.random() * 6)\n  await sleep(1000)\n  return n\n}",
